Third-party notices for echoir-core

This file lists the third-party work that echoir-core ports, converts, builds in, ships or depends
on. Section 3 covers tools that are not distributed. Sections 4 to 11 cover the libraries that the
built libraries, the echoir command line and the release archives contain. The full license texts
of these libraries ship in the licenses/ folder of every release archive and of the NuGet package.
In the repository, the libraries under third_party/ keep their license files next to them: the
submodules in their own trees, each single header with a `<name>.LICENSE.txt` file in
third_party/single/, and the Apache-2.0 and LLVM exception texts in third_party/licenses/.

1. FireRedVAD (code and weights)

   Authors:  FireRedTeam
   License:  Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/Apache-2.0.txt)
   Status:   Apache-2.0 is the license recorded for this work in models/registry.json and in the
             converted GGUF files. The upstream repository's LICENSE file is Apache-2.0 (checked
             on GitHub, 2026-10-29).

   Upstream sources
   - Code: https://github.com/FireRedTeam/FireRedVAD, commit
     c30ec49e8cc69642b0ee65362eba11b9d11c6e54
   - Weights: https://huggingface.co/FireRedTeam/FireRedVAD, revision
     7990aaccc6b7aec1e527743bd30201f2c4a03b8c (directories VAD/ and Stream-VAD/, each with
     model.pth.tar and cmvn.ark)

   Use in echoir-core
   - Network, feature front end and post-processor, written in C++ from the upstream code:
     src/vad/firered_model.{h,cpp} (the DFSMN network, on ggml), src/audio/fbank.{h,cpp} (the
     Kaldi front end and CMVN) and src/stream/vad_postprocess.{h,cpp} (the post-processor).
     src/vad/firered_vad.{h,cpp} wires them together.
   - tools/convert-firered-vad.py reads the upstream checkpoint layout and CMVN formula.
   - tools/dev/firered_reference.py calls the upstream Python code to write the reference data.
   - Weights: converted to GGUF by tools/convert-firered-vad.py. The converted files are hosted at
     https://huggingface.co/nanoshino/FireRedVAD-GGUF (firered-vad-v1.gguf and
     firered-stream-vad-v1.gguf), and tools/fetch-models.sh converts them locally from the
     upstream weights when the hosted files are not available. The converter writes
     general.license = "apache-2.0" and general.source.url into each file.
   - Reference data: tests/fixtures/firered/ holds outputs (features, probabilities and speech
     ranges) computed from the upstream code and weights.

2. Qwen3-ASR streaming decoder (algorithm)

   Authors:  Qwen team, Alibaba
   License:  Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/Apache-2.0.txt)
   Upstream: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-ASR, qwen_asr/inference/qwen3_asr.py
             (streaming_transcribe and its rollback parameters)

   Use in echoir-core
   - The rollback stream policy in src/stream/session.cpp and the prefix rollback in
     src/backends/qwen_backend.cpp follow the upstream scheme: the previous output, minus its last
     tokens, is the fixed start of the next decode, and the first decodes have no fixed start. The
     default counts (2 unfixed decodes, 5 rolled-back tokens) are the upstream defaults. No
     upstream code is copied; the scheme is written in C++ and applied per speech segment.

3. Reference implementations used by the development tools only (not vendored, not distributed)

   - kaldi-native-fbank (https://github.com/csukuangfj/kaldi-native-fbank), by csukuangfj. Its
     license is Apache License, Version 2.0 (checked on GitHub, 2026-10-29; the license text is in
     licenses/Apache-2.0.txt). It is installed in the development Python environment for the
     reference features.
   - torch, numpy, kaldiio, pyyaml and soundfile are needed by tools/dev/firered_reference.py. They
     are not part of this repository.

   src/audio/fbank.{h,cpp} implement the same Kaldi computation in C++ and are checked against
   those reference features. Their algorithm follows kaldi-native-fbank under the Apache-2.0
   license, as the header of src/audio/fbank.h says. The code is ours, and nothing is copied from
   kaldi-native-fbank.

